+`.env` uses the usual dotenv syntax: `KEY=value`, optional single or double quotes around the value, an optional leading `export `, and `#` comment lines. Unquoted values may end with an inline ` # comment`; a `#` inside quotes is kept as part of the value.
+
+## Diagnosing configuration
+
+`python -m payhook doctor` prints every setting with its effective value and where it came from (`env`, `.env` or `default`), plus the absolute path of the `.env` file it looked at. Secret values (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are never printed; only their length is shown. The output is safe to paste into a support ticket.
+
